(Bernadette:)So, what are you
working on these days?

2
00:00:04,939 --> 00:00:06,839
(Amy:)I'm studying
one-celled organisms

3
00:00:06,841 --> 00:00:08,041
(Amy:)to try and find
the neurochemicals

4
00:00:08,042 --> 00:00:09,612
(Amy:)that lead to the feeling
of shame.

5
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:12,950
(Bernadette:)What would a one-celled organism
have to be embarrassed about?

6
00:00:12,947 --> 00:00:16,277
(Penny:)Same as all of us, getting out
of a car without underwear.

7
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:19,121
(Bermadette:)Speaking of underwear,

8
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,950
(Bermadette:)I have some interesting news...

9
00:00:20,955 --> 00:00:23,125
(Penny:)Okay, if it's
sometimes Howie wears yours,

10
00:00:23,124 --> 00:00:24,124
(Penny:)Leonard already told us.

11
00:00:26,127 --> 00:00:28,527
(Bernadette:)He was being funny.

12
00:00:28,529 --> 00:00:30,099
(Bernadette:)I'm pretty sure.

13
00:00:31,799 --> 00:00:35,069
(Bernadette:)Anyway, I was asked to be
a part of a magazine article

14
00:00:35,069 --> 00:00:37,969
(Bernadette:)about the 50 sexiest female
scientists in California.

15
00:00:37,972 --> 00:00:39,172
(Bernadette:)Isn't that cool?

16
00:00:39,173 --> 00:00:40,843
(Amy:)I think it's awful.

17
00:00:40,841 --> 00:00:42,141
(Penny:)Why would you say that?

18
00:00:42,143 --> 00:00:45,143
(Amy:)Bernadette is a
successful microbiologist.

19
00:00:45,146 --> 00:00:47,876
(Amy:)She should be celebrated for
her achievements, not her looks.

20
00:00:47,882 --> 00:00:49,712
(Amy:)I mean, what kind of message
does that send?

21
00:00:49,717 --> 00:00:53,217
I think the message is-- "check
out the rack on that scientist."

22
00:00:55,156 --> 00:00:58,856
(Bernadette:)Why can't someone be thought
of as both smart and pretty?

23
